{
  "spec": "rogue-subtlety",
  "state": "written",
  "notes": "Subtlety at 60, hand-curated from simmed candidates (design/reviews/2026-10-07-rogue-curation.md). In the fight, Hemorrhage builds and keeps its Rupture-amplifying debuff up, Ghostly Strike goes on cooldown, Rupture is the main finisher whenever it has lapsed, and Death Mark (Eviscerate before you have it) and Slice and Dice spend the combo points that build while it runs. Every rank named here is checked against this build's own spellconst. 2026-10-31 (theorycraft audit fixes): Ambush moves from one second before the pull to the pull itself. The engine records no damage dealt before the pull, so the -1 s Ambush spent 60 Energy and its hit counted for nothing; at 0 s the rogue is still stealthed and the hit counts. 2026-11-02 guide rewrite: Garrote replaces Ambush after Premeditation (Initiative adds the fourth point; a bleed ignores the unsundered armor at the pull), +1.0% raid 60. Client 1.60.1.70755: Shank (1329283 at 24, 1329549 at 44; off-hand 50% weapon damage, 5 energy for +15/+25, 10 sec cooldown, cannot miss) is new for every rogue and is cast on cooldown right after the cooldowns line. Death Mark (1325758, the Subtlety capstone that replaced Thousand Cuts) goes right after the Rupture line, at five combo points with Rupture ticking (four from round 16). 2026-11-04 (round 16): Garrote goes back on after every Ghostly Strike, refreshing it, with Hemorrhage held while Ghostly Strike's 1329326 is up; Hemorrhage had starved the Garrote line of its 40 energy, so it ran about twice a fight.",
  "expected_idle": [
    {
      "id": 11294,
      "reason": "Sinister Strike is gated `not spellIsKnown(Hemorrhage/16511)`, the fallback builder for a bare build below Hemorrhage's talent row (Subtlety tier 4). At every level this ladder's own zero_casts check flags it, the truncated talent build has already spent points on Hemorrhage, so the gate correctly keeps Sinister Strike idle and lets Hemorrhage claim the builder slot instead -- the fallback yielding as designed, not a defect."
    },
    {
      "id": 11300,
      "reason": "Eviscerate is the finisher only before Death Mark (Subtlety's 31-point talent, taken at level 40): from then on every combo point left over after Rupture goes into Death Mark, which pays more for less energy, so Eviscerate is idle from level 40 by design. Below 40, on the ladder's bare rungs, energy is scarce enough that every set of combo points goes straight into Rupture, which is cast again as soon as it ends."
    },
    {
      "id": 6774,
      "reason": "Same as Eviscerate above: at level 20 (and, when it is learned, 30) no combo points are left over while Rupture is running."
    }
  ],
  "engineering_notes": {
    "5": "Fix round: the ladder's bare build has zero points in Hemorrhage below the level its tier is reachable (tier 4 of the Subtlety tree), leaving no combo-point builder at all -- the same auraIsKnown/spellIsKnown gate shape mage-fire uses for Improved Scorch (12873).",
    "2": "Previously starved entirely: Slice and Dice used to sit here instead, re-applying itself at currentComboPoints >= 1 with no floor, so it looped at 1-3 combo points forever and this line never saw five combo points."
  },
